# Compiled / generated
*.qmlc
node_modules/

# wrangler's local state and build scratch. `wrangler dev --local` writes
# miniflare's sqlite files and a bundled copy of the Worker under here; they
# are a cache of a local run, not source, and they name Durable Object
# instances from whatever last ran on somebody's laptop.
.wrangler/

# Cargo build directories, ANCHORED. This was a bare `target/` for the life of
# the repository, and an unanchored directory pattern matches at every depth —
# so `rimed/rime-backup-core/src/target/`, a SOURCE module holding the backup
# backends, was invisible to git. The crate declared `pub mod target;`, the
# whole module was untracked, and the branch that added it could not compile on
# any machine but the one that wrote it: about 40 KB of implementation, the
# filesystem and R2 targets, plus their tests.
#
# It is the same shape as `*.pem` swallowing the pinned Sigstore root in
# September — a rule written for build output that also matched something the
# build needs. Anchored here, so only a real cargo directory at a known path is
# ignored and a module named `target` is a normal source file again.
/target/
rimed/target/
installer/target/

# Build artifacts — disk and installer images (large, never versioned)
*.img
*.iso

# Signing material — PRIVATE KEYS NEVER IN REPO (see signing/README.md)
*.key
*.priv
*.pem
*.p12

# ...with one deliberate exception, because the rule above silently ate it.
# files/system/trust/fulcio-root.pem is a PUBLIC certificate — the pinned
# Sigstore root that a signing certificate must chain to — and it is shipped by
# Containerfile.base, which fails the build if its fingerprint is not the
# expected one. It is not signing material and there is no private half.
#
# It was committed once and did not arrive: `*.pem` matched it, `git status`
# said nothing, and the branch was green because the file existed untracked in
# the worktree that wrote it. On a clean checkout the file is absent, and under
# the shipped default (signature=enforce) a missing root is CouldNotRun, which
# REFUSES — so the omission would not have broken a feature, it would have
# stopped every machine in the fleet from updating. Negated by exact path
# rather than by directory, so the next .pem to land here is a decision.
!files/system/trust/fulcio-root.pem

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# agent worktrees (transient)
.claude/
output/

# Byte-compiled artefacts. check-labwc-keybinds is run with py_compile during
# development; its cache must never ship in the image build context.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# tests/run-clippy.sh builds here so it never shares a target dir with cargo test
/target-clippy/
rimed/target-clippy/

# Nix out-links
result
result-*
